<title>UK: Scottish nuclear reactor closed after fire - BBC.</title>
<headline>Scottish nuclear reactor closed after fire - BBC.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>A nuclear reactor in Scotland has been closed after a fire, the BBC said on Friday.</p>
<p>It said the blaze had broken out in the turbine hall of the reactor in Ayrshire.  </p>
<p>A spokesman for Scottish Nuclear, part of British Energy Plc , said later the was no immediate danger to staff or the public following the incident at the Hunterston reactor.</p>
<p>He said the fire had been extinguished and there was no radioactive leak, according to the BBC's Ceefax teletext service.</p>
<p>The reactor was expected to be back in use some time over the weekend.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
